{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And you shall be holy to Me, etc.</b> The reason for His saying <b>to Me</b> is explained according to the statement of Amoraim, may their memory be for blessing (Torat Kohanim ad loc.): Let a person not say, 'It is impossible regarding the flesh of a pig,' etc. — rather, it is possible and possible, but 'My Father in heaven,' etc. And this is what He says — <b>and you shall be holy to Me</b> — that you should be separated to Me for the sake of My commandments and not on account of the abhorrence of the forbidden thing. And therefore He juxtaposed this statement to the distinguishing of domesticated and wild animals, to allude to what I have written." "And His saying <b>for holy am I, HaShem</b>, etc., gives a reason for this commandment of distinguishing unclean animals: <b>for holy, etc., and I have separated you from the peoples to be Mine.</b> And the very matter of Israel's separation from the nations is the very same matter as your separation from unclean animals. Blessed is HaShem who has separated us from the impure — from man to beast to the bird of the sky:" "<b>Conclusion of the portion Kedoshim</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:58.016573756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}